diff --git a/docs/T5820_BF16.md b/docs/T5820_BF16.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8f28a15
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/T5820_BF16.md
@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@
+# T5820 CUDA BF16 KV prototype
+
+Base: `13eedf552417a6a791a7d13c6597e24300ee3a09`. This is an isolated development branch,
+not the installed Strata engine. No model weights are needed for its tests.
+
+`--kv bf16` selects storage ID 4, distinct from FP16 ID 0. Decode and prompt writers
+round FP32 directly to BF16 with round-to-nearest-even. NaNs stay quiet NaNs; signed
+zero, infinity and subnormals are retained according to BF16 rounding. Gather,
+host backing, residency copies, staging and ring restore move the raw bits.
+The existing FP16 and quantized paths retain their defaults.
+
+`KvStorage` is passed in shapes, state and pool descriptors. The process policy is
+set once before state creation; changing it while sessions or graphs exist is
+unsupported. An incompatible descriptor, cache format or configuration must fail.
+The existing session v1 layout already carries a format ID for every KV image and
+the configuration hash includes `kv`. ID 4 extends that enum without changing the
+file layout. FP16/BF16 image restoration in either direction is rejected.
+
+The default BF16 attention kernel loads BF16 as FP32 and uses FP32 online softmax.
+`STRATA_BF16_PREFILL_TC=1` opts into the experimental prompt kernel: BF16 Tensor Core
+QK with FP32 accumulation, then FP32 softmax and PV. Q is represented as BF16 high
+and residual components. K/V never pass through FP16. This path requires sm_80+
+and Flash-Next's 12 query heads per KV head. It is not a measured speed claim;
+the scalar implementation remains the default and the numerical reference.
+
+The CPU test oracle uses arithmetic scaling and ties-to-even, independently of the
+production bit-add encoder. CUDA conversion is also compared with NVIDIA's BF16
+intrinsic. Attention uses an independent FP64 oracle over BF16-rounded K/V.
+Frozen tolerances: each output error <= `1e-4 + 2e-3 * abs(reference)` and normalized
+RMS <= `1e-3`. The large V sentinel is 131072; therefore report relative/RMS errors
+alongside maximum absolute error.
+
+The model-free tests are:
+
+- `bf16_cpu_test`, `bf16_bits_cuda`: all BF16 encodings, tie neighbors and seeded FP32 bits.
+- `bf16_cuda_test`, `bf16_prompt_tc`: page sizes 1/4/512, permuted pages, chunks
+  1/17/4096, direct/batched append, host/stage/gather bits, both attention paths,
+  verification row dispatch, graph capture/replay with changed device step data.
+- `bf16_attention_2051`: full selection width against independent attention.
+- `bf16_prompt_4096`: 4096 causal query rows, each selecting at most 17 cells.
+  This tests batch sizing; it is not a full model prompt.
+- `bf16_stream_parity`, `bf16_stream_262144`: 32768 resident cells with 40000 or
+  262144 logical cells in one synthetic layer, CLOCK eviction, byte comparisons,
+  streaming graph replay after invalidation, and ring restore.
+- `bf16_state_test`: actual state allocation and MTP KV primitives with accept,
+  reject, partial commit, EOS/output limits, overwrite and ring restoration.
+  It does not run the weight-dependent MtpDrafter or Verifier.
+- `bf16_pin_failure`: real guarded pinned allocation with a 1 MiB injected limit,
+  including the host registration route. No residency/dtype fallback.
+- `bf16_fail_closed`: wrong pool dtype, unknown format and unsupported CLI combinations.
+- Extended conversation tests: BF16 snapshot/session metadata, restoration and
+  cross-dtype rejection. Existing FP16/INT8/Q4/hybrid tests remain regression checks.
+
+Unsupported combinations are rejected: batch slots, multi-GPU,
+elastic KV, rotated KV and native short FP16 attention. The separate setup/Terminal
+launchers do not expose BF16; use this engine only for approved prototype work.
+HIP, SYCL and Metal BF16 are not implemented or qualified.
+
+MTP shares the new append/read/ring functions. Its pinned allocation failure now
+ends BF16 initialization instead of switching to a fully resident cache. Rejected
+draft bytes can remain beyond the committed cursor, as upstream; selection bounds
+exclude them and subsequent writes replace them. Full MTP logits, acceptance,
+GDN/indexer commit integration and real conversation continuation require weights
+and are NOT RUN in this phase.
+
+DFlash2 currently has its own FP32 ring (5 default layers, 8 KV heads, dimension
+128, 2064 cells), FP32 temporary block K/V and a quantized feature history log.
+It is not BF16 merely because the target model uses BF16. Phase 2-B.1 permits
+`--kv bf16 --draft auto` with both drafter assets, `--spec >= 2` and an MTP fallback.
+The startup message explicitly reports target/MTP BF16 and DFlash2 FP32. Its own
+ring, block K/V, taps and feature scales retain their FP32 arithmetic; the feature
+log still uses INT8 codes and FP32 scales. No DFlash2 tensor aliases main KV.
+Strict BF16 target mode rejects drafter initialization and ring rebuild failures,
+and cross-target-dtype state copies. It does not silently load only MTP after a
+failed DFlash2 load. Legacy FP16 fallback behavior is retained. Session files
+persist main BF16 images with dtype ID 4; DFlash2 history is process-local and is
+not serialized as BF16. A session restored without its draft history may explicitly
+report a cold draft ring, whose proposals still require target verification.
+
+`bf16_dflash2_state` creates a 62,682,681-byte synthetic context-only pack in a
+temporary directory. It exercises real context projection, FP32 ring writes,
+lineage rewind/parking/branching/eviction, state copying, deferred tap replay,
+graph capture/replay, allocation errors, and unchanged BF16 main host/device
+sentinels. The fixture omits block/head/selector tensors; full draft inference and
+the request-level auto bandit are NOT RUN. Deferred 4+4-row and direct 8-row context updates must match bitwise. The inherited
+test fixture's default-stream pageable upload was corrected to use the drafter's
+nonblocking stream, so the consumer cannot read an unfinished upload. MTP KV
+mechanism tests remain required.
+`bf16_dflash2_race_smoke` exercises context/copy/graph and accepted/rejected
+prefixes with fewer than 64 projected rows, for resource-bounded shared-memory
+racecheck. Long lineage/rewind tests remain separate normal and memcheck cases.
+The T5820 validation runner limits racecheck to one worker, 100000 nonzero hazard
+records, a 6 GiB process-group RSS ceiling and an 8 GiB host-availability floor.
+Unbounded long-fixture racecheck exhausted the 64GB host and is not qualified.
+Shared-memory racecheck does not establish global DMA ordering; the explicit
+same-stream upload and bitwise regressions cover that boundary.
+Separate DFlash2/MTP hardware A/B tests decide performance after model approval.
+
+The T5820 delivery directory records toolchain/package hashes, build commands,
+binary hashes, executed test logs, sanitizer reports, and remaining resource gates.
+Synthetic success never qualifies IQ3_S at 256K. Model downloads, real inference,
+API deployment and the physical 96GB upgrade remain separate stages.
